{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfcU5VjtteB9HnxwApzWe", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's a regex for ISO 8601 calendar dates (`YYYY-MM-DD`):\n\n```\n^\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])$\n```\n\n- `\\d{4}` matches the year.\n- `(0[1-9]|1[0-2])` matches the month, 01\u201312.\n- `(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])` matches the day, 01\u201331.\n\nIt matches `2026-10-01`. It checks the format and ranges only, so it also accepts impossible dates like `2026-02-31`. Checking those needs a date parser. To find dates inside longer text, replace `^` and `$` with `\\b`."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7626, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16975, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7626}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "14ef760f-fe40-467b-b2f9-f7e1c22f75e9", "uuid": "b0c494a9-b788-43fe-ace6-47839f9c9bbb", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T00:31:19.964Z", "request_id": "req_011CfcU5VXVfzZ57HP3zVTxD"}
